    "text" : "This is the first of nine axial MRIs through the right ankle, presented from proximal to distal. The cut is just above the tibial plafond and is perpendicular to the long axis of the tibia. ​\n​\nThe anterior and posterior tibiofibular ligaments extend from the distal tibia to the fibula and, along with the interosseus ligament, support the distal tibiofibular joint. The anterior surface of the calcaneal (Achilles) tendon is flat. The tendon is partially surrounded by a para-tenon. The plantaris tendon is found just medial to the Achilles tendon.​\n​\nPosterior tibial and flexor digitorum longus tendons lie in a groove posterior to the medial malleolus. They are held in place by the overlying flexor retinaculum. The posterior tibial tendon is twice the diameter of the flexor digitorum longus tendon."
  },
  {
