ction, abnormalities in the brain and spine, diagnosis of knee injuries, and has eliminated the need for myelography. When used in areas such as the abdomen/pelvis and breast it has shown to have high sensitivity in detecting cancer. ​\n ​\nProton-density MRI is another MRI technique, where there is longer TR between two radiofrequency pulses and shorter TE. This technique is useful for detecting joint disease and injury."
