    "text" : "The nasopharynx is the most rostral portion of the pharynx, the musculomembranous part of the throat extending from the nasal cavity to the esophagus and larynx. \n\nThe nasopharynx is bounded by the nasal cavity (with which it communicates via the choanae), the base of the skull and the superior surface of the soft palate. \n\nBy contrast to the other parts of the pharynx, the nasopharynx always remains open to air flow, and is the only part of the pharynx involved in the respiratory, but not the digestive, system. The Eustachian tubes connect the inner ear to the nasopharynx, serving to equalize barometric pressure between the inner ear and the external environment."
  }
