[
  {
    "name" : "Quick Facts",
    "text" : "The capsules of atlanto-occipital joints surround the joint formed between the atlas bone of the cervical spine and the occipital bone of the skull. As with the rest of the joint capsules of the spine, the capsules of atlanto-occipital joint serve to stabilise the joint, affording them a limited range of movement. \n\nThey prevent dislocation of the vertebrae, and slipping of one vertebra over another during excessive shearing and rotation movements. They also provide lubrication and nourishment of the joint."
