    "text" : "The corona mortis is an anatomical variant arterial anastomosis located over the pubic ramus. It joins the obturator and external iliac or inferior epigastric arteries. \n\nThe term 'corona mortis' translates as \"crown of death\", indicating the importance of this structure in orthopedic surgery. Accidental damage to this structure can cause significant hemorrhaging which may be difficult to then achieve hemostasis. It must therefore be considered cautiously during surgery."
