  {
    "name" : "Variations",
    "text" : "The xiphoid process may be found to variably point in the same axis as the body or sternum, or more often, anteriorly deviated. The inferior tip of the xiphoid process may variably present a pointed, blunt, bifid, or hooked appearance. Foramina may be occasionally present in both the body of sternum and, more frequently, the xiphoid process."
