[
  {
    "name" : "Quick Facts",
    "text" : "The parotid lymph nodes are lymph nodes located proximal to the parotid gland. There are two groups of parotid lymph nodes, differentiated by their location with respect to the gland: deep parotid lymph nodes, and superficial lymph nodes.

The deep parotid lymph nodes are situated deep to the parotid gland and drain the nasal cavities and the nasopharynx.

The superficial parotid lymph nodes are situated superficial to the parotid glands, anterior to the ear, and drain the nose, nasal cavity, external acoustic meatus, tympanic cavity, and the lateral borders of the orbit.

Both the deep and superficial parotid lymph nodes drain to the superior deep cervical nodes, which themselves drain to the jugular trunks."
  }
]

