- muscles of thigh;

- muscles of leg;

- muscles of foot."}]

[{"name": "Structure/Morphology", "text": "The medial arcuate ligament is the arch-like, thickened area of the fascia covering the psoas major muscle. It attaches to the transverse process of the first lumbar vertebra, extends anteromedially across the anterior aspect of the psoas major muscle, and attaches to the anterolateral aspects of the vertebral bodies of the first and second lumbar vertebrae."}, {"name": "Anatomical Relations", "text": "There are five arcuate ligaments associated with the diaphragm:

- one median arcuate ligament;

- two medial arcuate ligaments;

- two lateral arcuate ligaments.

