[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The lingual surface is the aspect of the mandibular second premolar tooth that faces towards the tongue and oral cavity. It is one of five surfaces of the crown of the tooth, the other four being the buccal, mesial, distal, and occlusal surfaces.

