    "text" : "Inferior aspect of the posterior tubercle of the transverse process of seventh cervical vertebra"
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The inferior articular facets are the smooth, anterolaterally facing articular areas on the inferior articular processes of a lumbar vertebra. They articulate with the corresponding superior articular facets of the vertebra below, forming zygapophyseal joints."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The head is the expanded, pulley-shaped, distal end of the proximal phalanx of fourth toe. It is the distal continuation of its body and contains a distal articular facet, which articulates with the proximal articular facet of the middle phalanx of fourth toe, forming the proximal interphalangeal joint of the fourth toe.\n\nThe head of proximal phalanx of fourth toe provides attachment sites for the collateral, accessory collateral and plantar ligaments of the proximal interphalangeal joint of the fourth toe."
  }
]

[
