    "text" : "The bregma is a craniometric point found along the midline on the superior aspect of the cranium. It is formed by the frontal bone and the right and left parietal bones and is located at the area where the sagittal and coronal sutures meet.\n\nThe bregma is the location site for the anterior fontanelle in infants."
