    "text" : "The base is the expanded proximal end of the middle (intermediate) phalanx of the ring finger. It is the proximal continuation of its body and contains a proximal articular facet, which articulates with the distal articular facet of the proximal phalanx of the ring finger, forming the proximal interphalangeal joint of the ring finger. \n\nThe base of the middle phalanx of the ring finger provides an insertion site for the extensor digitorum muscle. It also provides attachment sites for the collateral and palmar ligaments for the proximal interphalangeal joint of the ring finger."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The vertex is a craniometric point found along the midline on the superior aspect of the cranium. It is the most superior point of the cranium, formed by both the right and left parietal bones, and is usually located along the sagittal suture."
