]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The body of ischium is the posteriorly located, thick, irregularly shaped part of the bone. It is one of the two parts of the ischium, the other being the ramus of ischium. Its superior portion fuses with the body of ilium and the superior pubic ramus and forms the posteroinferior two fifths of the acetabulum. Its inferior portion consists of the ischial tuberosity and the ramus of ischium extends anteromedial from this portion.

