- lateral: coracobrachialis muscle;

- medial: axillary vein."}, {"name": "Branches", "text": "There is one branch from the first part (proximal to the pectoralis minor muscle) of the axillary artery, the superior thoracic artery. It arises inferior to the subclavius and extends to the thoracic wall to anastomose with the internal thoracic artery.

