[{"name": "Description", "text": "The muscles of the circumorbital region attach proximally to the bony margin of the orbits. They are somatic, voluntary muscles belonging to the group of muscles of facial expression. Their distal attachments are to the skin and they are innervated by cranial nerve VII, the facial nerve. The actions of these muscles are closure of the eyelids, movement of the skin around the eye (including eyebrows), and compression of the lacrimal glands. They include:

—orbicularis oculi muscle; 

—corrugator supercilii muscle;

—depressor supercilii muscle."}, {"name": "References", "text": "Standring, S. (2016) Gray's Anatomy: The Anatomical Basis of Clinical Practice. Gray's Anatomy Series: Elsevier Limited."}]

