- head, which appears within the second to third years.

These ossification centers fuse with each other during the fifteenth to nineteenth years (Standring, 2016)."}, {"name": "Variations", "text": "In some individuals, the second metacarpal bone can present a pseudoepiphysis at its proximal end. It does not contribute greatly to the longitudinal growth of the bone and joins the body earlier than the epiphysis of the head (Tubbs, Shoja and Loukas, 2016)."}, {"name": "Surface Anatomy", "text": "The following bony features of the second metacarpal bone are relevant to surface anatomy:

