    "text" : "A bipolar neuron has one axon and one dendritic branch."
  },
  {
    "name" : "Anatomical Relations",
    "text" : "Bipolar neurons are very rare and only occur in organs of the special senses e.g., taste, smell sight, hearing and equilibrium. The specialized amacrine cell in the retina has no axon (Ross and Pawlina, 2016)."
  },
  {
    "name" : "Function",
    "text" : "Bipolar neurons are sensory neurons in organs of the special senses."
  },
  {
