Arterial Supply: Dorsal branches of posterior intercostal arteries."}, {"name": "Origin", "text": "The long rotatores muscles originate from the posterior aspects of the transverse processes of thoracic vertebrae. There can be variations between individuals regarding the origin sites for the long rotatores muscles."}, {"name": "Insertion", "text": "The fibers of the long rotatores muscles travel superomedially to the thoracic vertebrae that are located two vertebral segments superior to their origin sites, and insert onto the:

