[{"name": "Description", "text": "The deep gluteal muscles are one of two subgroups of muscles of the gluteal region, the other being the superficial gluteal muscles. Overall, these muscles mainly act to:

- abduct the thigh at the hip joint;

- laterally rotate the thigh at the hip joint.

The deep gluteal muscles consist of the:

- gemelli;

- obturator internus;

- piriformis;

- quadratus femoris."}]

