- helps steady the pelvis when the opposite foot is raised off the ground during walking and running.

The gluteus medius muscle can be tested by medially rotating the thigh at the hip joint against resistance while lying in the supine position with both the hip and knee joints flexed, during which it can be palpated (Standring, 2016)."}, {"name": "List of Clinical Correlates", "text": "- Trendelenburg sign"}, {"name": "References", "text": "Standring, S. (2016) Gray's Anatomy: The Anatomical Basis of Clinical Practice. Gray's Anatomy Series 41st edn.: Elsevier Limited."}]

