    "text" : "The internal surface (inner surface) of tenth rib is its smooth, concave, inner area. It is one of the two surfaces of the body of the tenth rib, the other being the external surface.\n\nThe internal surface of tenth rib consists of the costal groove, which is located on its inferior edge, adjacent to the ribs inferior border. It provides attachment sites for the subcostal and innermost intercostal muscles, and is covered by endothoracic fascia."
  }
]

