[{"name": "Quick Facts", "text": "Apical fibers are fibers of the periodontal ligament extending from the cementum to the fundus of the alveolus (Dorland, 2011)."}, {"name": "Structure and/or Key Feature(s)", "text": "There are five fiber types in the alveolodental ligament: 

