    "text" : "Anteriorly, the tendon of levator palpebrae superioris broadens and thins to form the levator aponeurosis. This aponeurosis has been described as bilaminar, with superficial and deep laminae.\n\nThe fibers of the superficial lamina radiate and pass through the orbicularis oculi muscle to attach to the skin of the upper eyelid. The fibers of the deep lamina attach to the anterior surface of the superior tarsal plate of the upper eyelid. These fibers are accompanied by the smooth muscle fibers of the superior tarsal muscle."
  },
  {
