]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The superior orbital fissure is a large cleft found along the posterior wall of each orbit. It is located lateral to the optic canal and superior to the foramen rotundum and inferior orbital fissure.

The margins of each superior orbital fissure are formed:

—medially, by the body of sphenoid bone;

—superiorly, by a lesser wing of sphenoid bone;

—inferolaterally, by a greater wing of sphenoid bone.

The superior orbital fissure allows for the passage of the oculomotor, trochlear, and abducens nerves, the ophthalmic nerve and its branches, and the superior and inferior ophthalmic veins."
  }
]

[
