[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The vaginal processes are the two bony plates that extend medially from the upper margins of both the right and left medial plates of the pterygoid processes of sphenoid bone. On its corresponding side, each vaginal process is located anterior to a pterygoid tubercle and lateral to the sphenoidal rostrum and articulates:\n\n—anteriorly, with a sphenoidal process of palatine bone;\n\n—posteriorly, with the superior border of vomer, contributing to the formation of the sphenovomerine suture."
