[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The frontolacrimal suture (lacrimofrontal suture) is a fibrous joint found along the anterolateral aspect of the cranium. It is the articulation site located between the orbital part of the frontal bone and the superior border of the lacrimal bone."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The transverse palatine suture is a fibrous joint that separates the anterior three quarters of the bony hard palate from its posterior one quarter. It is the articulation site located between the palatine processes of both the right and left maxillae and the horizontal plates of both the right and left palatine bones."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The internasal suture is a fibrous joint found along the anterior aspect of the cranium. It is the articulation site located between the medial borders of both the right and left nasal bones."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The inferior articular processes (inferior zygapophyses) are the two downwardly projecting processes located at the lateral parts of the vertebral arch of a thoracic vertebra. They extend inferiorly from the laminae.\n\nOverall, the inferior articular processes of thoracic vertebrae generally consist of inferior articular facets that face anteriorly and slightly medially. They articulate with the superior articular processes of the vertebra below, forming zygapophyseal joints."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The short limb (short process or short crus) of incus is the small, superomedial projection of the bone. It is continuous inferolaterally with the body of incus and provides an attachment site for the posterior ligament of incus."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The internal surface (inner surface) of fourth rib is its smooth, concave, inner area. It is one of the two surfaces of the body of the fourth rib, the other being the external surface.\n\nThe internal surface of fourth rib consists of the costal groove, which is located on its inferior edge, adjacent to the ribs inferior border. It provides an insertion site for the transversus thoracis muscle, attachment sites for the innermost intercostal muscles, and is covered by endothoracic fascia."
  }
]

