[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The head of third metatarsal bone is the expanded, rounded, distal end of the bone. It is the distal continuation of its body, contains a distal articular facet, and provides attachment sites for the collateral, accessory collateral and plantar ligaments of the third metatarsophalangeal joint."
  }
