    "text" : "The occlusal (masticatory) surface is the aspect of the maxillary second molar tooth that faces the teeth of the mandibular dental arcade and comes into contact with them (occlusion) during mastication. It is one of the five surfaces of the crown of the tooth, the other four being the buccal, lingual, mesial, and distal surfaces. The occlusal surface consists of:

