    "text" : "The internal surface (endocranial surface) is the smooth, concave area found along the inner aspect of the squamous part of frontal bone. It is one of two surfaces of the squamous part of frontal bone, the other being the external surface. \n\nThe internal surface consists of the frontal crest, the anterior portion of the groove for the superior sagittal sinus, and impressions that accommodate the frontal lobes of the cerebrum.\n\nThe internal surface provides an attachment site for the falx cerebri."
