    "text" : "The superior border (superior margin or petrous ridge) is the long margin found along the upper aspect of the petrous part of temporal bone. It is one of the three borders of the petrous part of temporal bone, the other two being the anterior and posterior borders, and it separates its anterior and posterior surfaces.

The superior border:

—extends posterolaterally from the apex of petrous part of temporal bone towards the superior end of the groove for sigmoid sinus on the temporal bone;

—consists of the groove for superior petrosal sinus;

