[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The greater horns (greater cornua) are the two thin, oblique, posterolaterally located parts of the hyoid bone. On its corresponding side, each greater horn of hyoid bone:

—extends posterosuperiorly from a lateral end of the body of hyoid bone; 

—is continuous superomedially with a lesser horn of hyoid bone;

