[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The lateral border is the margin found along the anterolateral aspect of the body of ischium. It is one of the three borders of the body of ischium, the other two being the anterior and posterior borders, and it separates the femoral and dorsal surfaces of the body of ischium. It forms the lateral margin of the ischial tuberosity and travels superiorly towards the acetabular margin.\n\nThe lateral border of body of ischium provides an attachment site for the ischiofemoral ligament."
  }
