    "text" : "The anterior border (anterior margin) is the short margin found along the anteroinferior aspect of the petrous part of temporal bone. It is one of the three borders of the petrous part of temporal bone, the other two being the posterior and superior borders, and it separates its anterior and inferior surfaces.

The anterior border:

—extends laterally from the apex of petrous part of temporal bone towards the sphenoidal border of the squamous part of temporal bone;

—articulates anteriorly with the greater wing of sphenoid bone, forming the sphenopetrosal synchondrosis."
