[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The cruciform eminence is the cross-shaped arrangement found along the internal surface of the squamous part of occipital bone. It consists of the:

—groove for the superior sagittal sinus, which forms its superior vertical line;

—internal occipital crest and groove for the occipital sinus, which together form its inferior vertical line;

—right and left grooves for transverse sinuses, which form its right and left horizontal lines, respectively;

—internal occipital protuberance, which is located at its center.

The cruciform eminence divides the internal surface of the squamous part of occipital bone into four fossae:

—two superiorly located cerebral fossae;

—two inferior located cerebellar fossae."
