    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The inferior angle of scapula is the blunt area of the bone where its medial and lateral borders meet. It is located superficial to the seventh rib or the seventh intercostal space and is one of the three angles of the scapula, the other two being the superior and lateral angles.\n\nThe inferior angle of scapula provides an insertion site for the serratus anterior muscle."
