[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The acetabular margin (border or rim) is the prominent edge surrounding the acetabulum. It is the site of attachment for the fibrocartilaginous acetabular labrum, which serves to deepen the cavity that the acetabulum provides for the head of femur in order to reinforce the hip joint.\n\nThe acetabular margin has an inferiorly located gap, known as the acetabular notch, which allows for the passage of nerves and vessels into the hip joint."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The cervical line (cementoenamel junction) is a thin, irregular margin that forms the boundary between the enamel covering the crown and the cementum covering the root. Therefore, the cervical line separates the crown and root of the tooth."
  }
]

