[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The anatomical neck of humerus is the short, constricted part of the bone that connects the head and body of the humerus. It is formed by a shallow groove, which encircles the head of the humerus. \n\nThe anatomical neck of humerus separates the head from the greater and lesser tubercles. It provides an attachment site for the capsule of the glenohumeral (shoulder) joint."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The nasal margin (nasal notch) is the serrated border found along the anteroinferior aspect of the nasal part of frontal bone. It articulates:\n\n—medially, with the superior borders of both the right and left nasal bones, forming the frontonasal suture;\n\n—laterally, with the frontal processes of both the right and left maxillae, forming the frontomaxillary sutures."
  }
]

[{"name": "Description", "text": "The levator ani muscle is one of the two muscles of the pelvic diaphragm, the other being the ischiococcygeus. It forms a large part of the pelvic diaphragm, which supports the pelvic organs. The levator ani muscle is a combined term for three muscles, these are the:

- iliococcygeus;

- pubococcygeus;

- puboanalis.

The levator ani muscle can be arbitrarily divided, by the midline of the body, into right and left halves."}]

[
  {
