[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The vertebral body is the anteriorly located cylindrical part of the eighth thoracic vertebra. When viewed from above, it appears heart-shaped. Its anterior aspect is concave, while its posterior aspect, which forms the anterior wall of the vertebral foramen, is flat. It is connected to the vertebral arch via two pedicles, which extend from the upper corners of its posterior aspect. It consists of:

