[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The posterior surface is the area on the posterosuperior aspect of the petrous part of temporal bone. It is one of three surfaces of the petrous part of temporal bone, the other two being the anterior and inferior surfaces. It is an area that is bounded:

—anterosuperiorly, by the superior border of the petrous part of temporal bone;

—posteroinferiorly, by the inferior border of the petrous part of temporal bone.

The posterior surface consists of the subarcuate fossa and internal acoustic meatus. It contributes to the formation of the posterior cranial fossa."
