    "text" : "The frontal eminences (frontal tuber or frontal tuberosity) are the two prominent, round, anterolaterally located areas on the external surface of the squamous part of frontal bone. They are each found superior to the superciliary arches and are areas of the frontal bone where its convexity is at its maximum."
