    "text" : "The groove for greater petrosal nerve is a small, shallow depression found along the anterior surface of the petrous part of temporal bone. It is located:

—anterior to the arcuate eminence;

—medial to the groove for lesser petrosal nerve;

—lateral to the trigeminal impression.

The groove travels anteromedially from the hiatus of greater petrosal nerve to the foramen lacerum. The greater petrosal nerve passes through this groove."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The pterygoid foveae (pterygoid pits) are the two small, shallow depressions found along the anterior aspect of each neck of the mandible. On its corresponding side, each pterygoid fovea provides an insertion site for a lateral pterygoid muscle."
  }
