[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The obelion is a craniometric point found along the midline on the superior aspect of the cranium. It is formed by both the right and left parietal bones and is located at the area along the sagittal suture that lies between the right and left parietal foramina."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The lateral epicondyle (external epicondyle) of humerus is the projection found at the distal end of the lateral supracondylar ridge. It is less prominent than the medial epicondyle of the humerus.\n\nThe lateral epicondyle provides origin sites for the superficial group of muscles of the posterior compartment of forearm and the supinator and anconeus muscles. It also provides an attachment site for the radial collateral ligament."
