[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The parietal margins (parietal borders) are the beveled borders found along the superolateral aspects of both the right and left greater wings of the sphenoid bone. On its corresponding side, each parietal margin articulates with the sphenoidal angle of a parietal bone, forming a sphenoparietal suture."
