[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The anterior border (margin) of humerus is the margin located along the frontal aspect of the body of the humerus. It extends inferiorly from the crest of the greater tubercle to the coronoid fossa and separates the anteromedial and anterolateral surfaces of the humerus."
  }
]

[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The infraorbital foramen is the small, round, superiorly located openings found along the anterior surfaces of each maxilla. It is located inferior to the orbit, superior to the canine fossa, and lateral to the piriform aperture of the nose.\n\nEach infraorbital foramen forms the inferior opening of the infraorbital canal and allows for the passage of the infraorbital artery, vein, and nerve."
