    "text" : "The superior intervertebral surface is the flat, rough area on the upper aspect of the body of a thoracic vertebra. It is surrounded by a smooth outer rim, known as the superior annular epiphysis.\n\nOverall, the intervertebral surfaces of vertebrae provide attachment sites for the intervertebral discs. Adjacent vertebral bodies articulate with each other via intervertebral discs, forming the intervertebral symphysis joints."
