[
  {
    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The posterior border of ulna is the subcutaneous margin located along the dorsal aspect of the body of ulna. It extends inferiorly from the olecranon to the ulnar styloid process.\n\nThe posterior border of ulna separates the medial and posterior surfaces of the ulna and provides an origin site for the flexor carpi ulnaris and extensor carpi ulnaris muscles."
  }
