    "text" : "The head of fifth rib is the round, expanded, posterior part of the bone. It is the medial continuation of its neck.\n\nIt consists of superior and inferior articular facets, which are separated from each other by its crest. These articular facets articulate with the bodies of the adjacent thoracic vertebrae, forming the joint of the head of the fifth rib."
  }
]

