    "name" : "Description",
    "text" : "The vertebral body is the small, anteriorly located cylindrical part of the fifth cervical vertebra. Its anterior aspect is concave, while its posterior aspect, which forms the anterior wall of the vertebral foramen, is flat. Both its superior and inferior surfaces are saddle-shaped. The pedicles extend from its posterolateral aspects and the anterior roots of the transverse processes extend from its lateral aspects. It consists of:

