    "text" : "Fibers of the inferior mesenteric plexus are derived from the intermesenteric plexus and inferior mesenteric ganglion. From this plexus arise several subsidiary plexuses that extend along the arterial branches of the inferior mesenteric artery to innervate targets that those arterial branches supply.\n\nThe left branches of the inferior mesenteric plexus travel with the left colic arteries to innervate them and the descending colon."
