    "text" : "Fibers of the superior mesenteric plexus are derived from the celiac plexus and superior mesenteric ganglion. From this plexus arise a number of subsidiary plexuses that extend along the arterial branches of the superior mesenteric artery to innervate targets that those arterial branches supply.\n\nThe middle colic branches of the superior mesenteric plexus travel with the middle colic and marginal arterial branches to innervate them and the transverse colon, along with parts of the ascending and descending colon."
  }
]

