    "text" : "The longitudinal layer of muscle fibers is thicker than the circular layer and form the outer layer of the muscularis externa. It extends the entire length of the esophagus, except posterosuperiorly, where it merges as two fascicles that ascend to the lower border of the inferior constrictor and ends as a tendon attaching to the posterior ridge of the cricoid lamina."
  },
  {
    "name" : "Function",
