    "text" : "The mesiobuccal cusp is the superiorly located, pointed elevation found along the mesiobuccal aspect of the crown of mandibular third molar tooth. It is one of the four cusps of this tooth, the other three being the mesiolingual, distobuccal, and distolingual cusps. The mesiobuccal cusp consists of both cusp and triangular ridges."
  }
]

[
  {
